title: We can imprison Leuchtenberg.
subtitle: He is a criminal, after all.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if judicial_reform < 2 : Unfortunately, the reactionary judiciary will not cooperate. ?] [? if presidential_election_seen == 1 : Hitler has already been made a citizen of Germany, in the run-up to the presidential election. ?] [? if not rsdrp_prussia : We cannot do this without the cooperation of the Prussian police, who are not currently in our control. ?]
view-if: nazi_urgency >= 3 and hitler_deported = 0 and chancellor != "Papen" and chancellor != "Schleicher" and investigate_far_right >= 2
choose-if: judicial_reform >= 2 and presidential_election_seen == 0 and rsdrp_prussia == 1

Is it really that simple? Won't his supporters react violently to this suggestion? And even if the imprisonment does succeed, won't he just beg to the courts, or perhaps organize from prison? And, some people consider this to be an anti-democratic abuse of power, using the law in order to target a political opponent.

- @deport: Imprison him!
- @no_deport: No, we must not.

@deport
go-to: deport_violence if sa_strength >= 200; deport_success if sa_strength < 200

@deport_violence

When the police approach, he is surrounded by his SRNM guards, preventing him from being detained! We can attempt to force a confrontation, but that may have negative consequences. The SF may also attempt to draw off the SRNM.

- @force_approach: Force the approach!
- @no_deport: Cancel the deportation.

@force_approach
on-arrival: {!
var total_allied_strength = Q.rb_strength*Q.rb_militancy + Q.prussian_police_strength*Q.prussian_police_militancy*Q.prussian_police_loyalty;
var enemy_strength = Q.sa_strength*Q.sa_militancy;
console.log('Deporting Hitler - force approach');
console.log(total_allied_strength, enemy_strength);

if (total_allied_strength > enemy_strength) {
    Q.deportation_success = 1;
} else {
    Q.deportation_success = 0;
}
!}
go-to: force_fail if deportation_success == 0; force_success if deportation_success = 1

@force_fail
on-arrival: sa_strength += 50; workers_nts += 5; unemployed_nts += 5; new_middle_nts += 5; old_middle_nts += 5; rural_nts += 5; coup_progress += 3

Unfortunately, our forces fail to disloge the SRNM from their positions surrounding Leuchtenberg. He is seen as both a strong and powerful leader and a victim, further reinforcing his image. The Solidarists are left stronger than ever.

@force_success
on-arrival: hitler_deported = 1; sa_strength = sa_strength/2; workers_nts -= 10; new_middle_nts -= 10; old_middle_nts -= 10; rural_nts -= 10; unemployed_nts -= 10; sa_banned = 1; coup_progress -= 2; nts_leader = "Goebbels"
achievement: deport_hitler

The confrontation ends with the police and Soyuz prevailing, capturing Leuchtenberg so he can be jailed! This is a sign of weakness, and his physical distance makes organizing difficult, impeding the Solidarist effort to win more votes.

In Leuchtenberg's absence, Viktor Baidalakov has become the temporary leader of the NTS, with substantial influence from Alexander Galich.

@deport_success
on-arrival: hitler_deported = 1; sa_strength = sa_strength/2; workers_nts -= 10; new_middle_nts -= 10; old_middle_nts -= 10; rural_nts -= 10; unemployed_nts -= 10; coup_progress -= 2; nts_leader = "Goebbels"
achievement: deport_hitler

Somehow, the plan worked! There was minimal resistance to Leuchtenberg's deportation. This is a sign of weakness, and his physical distance makes organizing difficult, impeding the Solidarist effort to win more votes.

In Leuchtenberg's absence, Viktor Baidalakov has become the temporary leader of the NTS, with substantial influence from Alexander Galich.

@no_deport
go-to: root

We will not be detaining Leuchtenberg.
